sections.technical:
Specifically, the actors may exploit these flaws through multiple vectors:


 Authentication bypass;

 Arbitrary code injection; and

 Weak configurations. The actors may exploit vulnerabilities or weaknesses in unpatched or internet-accessible controllers to remotely alter settings and force units into continuous heating and defrost cycles, which can cause widespread inventory loss and equipment hazards. Upon successful exploitation of the flaws, the actors could achieve the following effects:


 Change of temperature, which could:


 Affect the service life of the system;

 Create a fire hazard;

 Cause loss of inventory; or

 Indirectly harm consumers if products are consumed after unsafe storage. Enforce credential security : Change default passwords [ CPG 3.A ], strengthen passwords, and implement strong password policies [ CPG 3.B ].
